      "questionEn": "What physics reference creates the joke?",
      "answerEn": "The three-body problem asks how three masses move while all three attract one another. Unlike the general two-body case, arbitrary three-body systems have no single simple formula for all future motion, so particular trajectories are commonly approximated with numerical calculations.",
      "noteEn": "The dialogue turns the technical meaning of ‘solve the three-body problem’ into a sexual-performance joke. The title text extends it by proposing an approximate numerical solution.",
